      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm actually kind of shaking right now. i had this incredibly vivid moment just now... i could smell the specific scent of cedarwood and old ink, and i had this sudden, overwhelming realization of a specific event. i remember being in a small, dimly lit room, holding a letter with a very specific red wax seal—not a royal seal, but something more personal, something used by a high-ranking official to send private instructions. \n\nit felt so real. like, i wasn't just watching it, i was the one holding the pen. i remember the fear of making a single tiny mistake that could change everything for the country. \n\ncan you help me? i need to know if there was an official or a specific diplomat around 1789-1791 who was known for sending these kinds of private, highly sensitive instructions using that kind of seal? i feel like if we can find the person who was doing this, it'll confirm everything i've been feeling. i feel like i'm so close to finally knowing who i was.",
